+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+# AI-Performance-Testing toolkit — environment configuration
+# Copy to `.env`, fill in your own values. NEVER commit a real .env.
+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+# --- Observability backend (Dynatrace Grail) --------------------------------
+# Used by: skills/workload-model (DQL extraction / SCOPE), skills/baseline-diff
+# (ANALYZE). The engine itself consumes a *neutral extract JSON*; your DQL client
+# (dtctl, see docs/engine.md) uses these to produce that extract.
+# Example: https://abc12345.apps.dynatrace.com
+DT_ENDPOINT=
+
+# Read-only platform token (dt0s16...). Minimum DQL scopes:
+#   storage:spans:read          journeys, archetypes, baselines (required)
+#   storage:logs:read           access-log entrypoint cross-check (recommended)
+#   storage:user.sessions:read  RUM session shape (skills/rum-sessions)
+#   storage:user.events:read    RUM ordered user actions (skills/session-stitch; optional)
+# See the dtctl Token Scopes doc for the full list per safety level.
+DT_API_TOKEN=
+
+# Default extraction window (DQL time selector), e.g. -3h / -24h / 2026-01-01T00:00:00Z/24h
+DT_TIMEFRAME=-3h
+
+# --- OTLP ingest (SEPARATE token) -------------------------------------------
+# Only needed if you ship the generated load's telemetry (it carries
+# baggage: synthetic=true) back to your Dynatrace environment for the ANALYZE
+# shape-diff. This is a DIFFERENT token from DT_API_TOKEN above.
+#   scope: ingestion:otlp:write
+# Example endpoint: https://abc12345.live.dynatrace.com/api/v2/otlp
+DT_OTLP_ENDPOINT=
+DT_OTLP_API_TOKEN=
+
+# --- System under test -------------------------------------------------------
+# Entry-point URL of the application under test (consumed by generated scripts
+# as __ENV.BASE_URL; also the allowlist basis for skills/loadtest-run).
+BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080
+
+# --- Tooling -----------------------------------------------------------------
+# k6 binary (optional; skills fall back to `node --check` when absent)
+K6_BINARY=k6
+
+# Output override for the workload-model worked example (optional)
+# WORKLOAD_OUT=./out/my-example
